    old "One by one he explained to Sarah what to use, how to use it, when to use it."
    new "Uno a uno le explicó a Sarah qué usar, cómo hacerlo y cuándo."

    old "He explained a strict routine of excercise and diet that she would have to obey to the letter."
    new "Explicó una rutina estricta de ejercicio y dieta que tendría que obedecer al pie de la letra."

    old "After he finished explaining her the routine, he pointed towards his belt and loincloth, still where he had left them."
    new "Después de terminar de explicarle la rutina, señaló hacia su cinturón y su faja, que aún estaban donde los había dejado."

    old "Fetch that for me."
    new "Tráelo por mí."

    old "Sarah obeyed her new mentor."
    new "Sarah obedeció a su nuevo mentor."

    old "She picked up the belt and loincloth and tried handing them back to Atilla."
    new "Sarah tomó el cinturón y la faja, intentando devolverlos a Atilla."

    old "He didn't not grab them."
    new "Sí que los agarró."

    old "It's not going to put itself on..."
    new "No va a ponerse por sí solo..."

    old "She grabbed the belt by both ends and tried to loop it around the orc's waist."
    new "Agarró el cinturón con ambas manos e intentó anudarlo alrededor de la cintura del orco."

    old "With his large size, Sarah could barely get her hands around his waists as she tried to fasten the belt back on him."
    new "Con su gran tamaño, Sarah apenas podía rodear sus caderas con las manos mientras intentaba abrocharle el cinturón de nuevo."

    old "She pressed her face into his chest. It felt like steel."
    new "Presionó su rostro contra su pecho. Se sentía como acero."

    old "Below, pressing against her stomach, she could feel his large member."
    new "Debajo, presionando contra su vientre, podía sentir su gran polla."

    old "Finally, she managed to loop the belt and close the buckle, making the orc decent again. As decent as he was ever going to be."
    new "Finalmente, logró enhebrar la correa y cerrar la hebilla, haciendo que el orco volviera a ser digno. Tan digno como jamás lo sería."

    old "Atilla gave his belt a tug, pleased at her work."
    new "Atilla tiró de su cinturón, complacido con su trabajo."

    old "He turned around and continued his lecture."
    new "Continuó su lección con calma, indiferente."

    old "Sarah studiously followed him and absorbed his lessons."
    new "Sarah siguió a su maestro con devoción y asimiló sus lecciones."
